#!/usr/bin/python3
"""The guide's recorder (DVR): records channels to disk, on this computer.

    om-pg-dvr drives              removable drives: {"drives": [{device, label, uuid, fstype, size, mount, free, ro}]}
    om-pg-dvr check <folder>      whether a folder can hold recordings, and what it is
    om-pg-dvr prepare <folder>    makes "Uber TV Recordings" in it, with its marker: the place to keep
                                  (prepare <folder> make: the folder too, if it's missing and in your home folder)
    om-pg-dvr where               a kept place (JSON on stdin), checked: {problem, path, free, size}
    om-pg-dvr mount <device>      mounts a drive from that list (udisksctl; no password in your session)
    om-pg-dvr start               starts a recording, its details as JSON on stdin (with "slot": a
                                  scheduled one that's due, claimed: it starts once, whoever asks)
    om-pg-dvr schedule            schedules shows ({"slots": [...]} on stdin): each one Scheduled, or a
                                  Conflict when as many as may record at once would be recording then
    om-pg-dvr series add          a series rule (channel and title, JSON on stdin): Record every episode
    om-pg-dvr series remove <id>  stops recording a series: its rule, and its shows not started yet
    om-pg-dvr cancel <id>         cancels a scheduled one (an episode of a series isn't scheduled again)
    om-pg-dvr limit <1-4>         how many may record at once (2 unless you say): one past it doesn't
                                  start, a scheduled one past it is a Conflict; one running goes on
    om-pg-dvr clear               takes every scheduled one off the list (Recordings turned off): the
                                  series rules stay, and schedule again once it's back on
    om-pg-dvr follow              a running recording's channel at a new address (JSON on stdin: a playlist
                                  that turned its links): it moves to it, the same file going on
    om-pg-dvr tag                 a show joined to the recording running on its channel (JSON on stdin:
                                  Record every episode on a show that's recording already): its stop moved
                                  to the show's end, its title, episode and series kept with it
    om-pg-dvr stop <id>           stops one (what's recorded is kept)
    om-pg-dvr until <id> <time>   changes when one stops (Unix seconds)
    om-pg-dvr list                every recording, scheduled ones too, and the series rules (never a stream's address)
    om-pg-dvr remove <id>         deletes one: its file, its details file, its picture
    om-pg-dvr run <id>            the recording itself; systemd runs it
    om-pg-dvr buffer start        pause and rewind for the channel being watched ({"url", "minutes": 5 or 30,
                                  "place", "keepFree", "height"} on stdin): {session, base}, once it's serving
    om-pg-dvr buffer stop <id>    stops a session, answering once its writer is gone; its folder is deleted
    om-pg-dvr buffer follow <id>  a session's channel at a new address (JSON on stdin), the old one closed first
    om-pg-dvr buffer-run <id>     the session itself; systemd runs it

Every answer is one line of JSON: {"ok": true, ...} or {"ok": false, "error": <code>}.

A place is kept as the filesystem it's on (its UUID, or what's mounted)
plus the "Uber TV Recordings" folder in it, which holds a marker file (My
Videos skips folders with one). Before every recording, and before one
plays, the place is checked again: the same filesystem, mounted where it
was, the folder really a folder. Anything else is "drive", and nothing is
written: a drive that's gone never sends a recording to the computer's own
disk.

A show scheduled for later waits in the state as Scheduled (or as a
Conflict, naming the others, when as many as may record at once would
already be recording then: the ones scheduled first keep their place). The guide's checker starts it when
it's due, with its channel's address looked up then (never kept with the
schedule); one the guide never got to (logged out, asleep, off) is Missed. Folders that are hidden, Uber TV's or your settings' own, the
system's, or in memory (tmpfs and the like) are refused.

Each recording is its own systemd user service (uber-tv-rec-<id>), so it
goes on with Uber TV closed and through a restart of the shell, while you
stay logged in. It holds a sleep inhibitor while it runs ("Recording TV"),
stops at its stop time (12 hours at most), stops early when the disk would
get fuller than the free space you keep, and says how it went in an Omarchy
notification. IPTV and YouTube live are copied as they come, never
converted, into MPEG-TS (a file cut short still plays), through a relay on
127.0.0.1 (lib/dvrproxy.py), so a stream's address, which can hold a
provider's login, is never on a command line; ffmpeg may follow http and
https only. A scheduled YouTube channel's show is a video: it's saved
whole, by yt-dlp, as .mkv. yt-dlp never reads your config or plugins.

Pause and rewind keeps the last 5 or 30 minutes of the channel being watched
in a folder at the recordings place (.uber-tv-buffer/<session>, yours alone
where the drive allows), each session its own systemd user service
(uber-tv-buf-<id>). It copies through the same relay, writes through the
folder's descriptor (a drive that's gone fails, never sends it to the
computer's own disk), stops before the drive gets fuller than you keep, and
serves the guide's player on 127.0.0.1 under a secret path
(lib/dvrbuffer.py). The guide asking for its status is its lease: without
it for 20 seconds (the shell gone), the session stops and deletes its folder.

The state (what's recording, what's been recorded and where) is
~/.config/om-pg/dvr/state.json, yours alone, changed only under its lock
file. A stream's address is kept there only while its recording runs. The
details file next to each recording has what's shown on its card and a
SHA-256 of its channel's address (for the channel lock), never the address.
"""

import contextlib
import errno
import fcntl
import hashlib
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import signal
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True   # the plugin's folder is watched: a .pyc written in lib/ would reload the guide

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
FFMPEG = "/usr/bin/ffmpeg"
FFPROBE = "/usr/bin/ffprobe"
THUMBNAILER = "/usr/bin/ffmpegthumbnailer"
YTDLP = "/usr/bin/yt-dlp"
SYSTEMD_RUN = "/usr/bin/systemd-run"
SYSTEMCTL = "/usr/bin/systemctl"
INHIBIT = "/usr/bin/systemd-inhibit"
SLEEP = "/usr/bin/sleep"
NOTIFY = "/usr/bin/notify-send"
LSBLK = "/usr/bin/lsblk"
UDISKSCTL = "/usr/bin/udisksctl"
PYTHON = "/usr/bin/python3"

ROOT_NAME = "Uber TV Recordings"
MARKER = ".uber-tv-recordings"
UNIT = "uber-tv-rec-"
ACTIVE = ("starting", "recording")
WAITING = ("scheduled", "conflict")   # not started: a schedule, or one that won't fit
KINDS = ("iptv", "youtube-live", "youtube-video")
QUALITIES = (1080, 720, 480)
MAX_HOURS = 12
AT_ONCE = (1, 2, 3, 4)             # how many may record at once (the guide's setting; 2 unless it says)
MAX_RECORDINGS = 5000
MAX_RULES = 200
MAX_SKIP = 200                     # a series' episodes you cancelled, so it doesn't schedule them again
MIN_SHOW = 300                     # the shortest show that's scheduled or joined: 5 minutes
MAX_IDS = 160                      # the shows one recording can hold: 12 hours of shows of 5 minutes or more
MAX_RULES_HELD = 160               # the series they can be of (one each)
MAX_AHEAD = 8 * 86400              # how far ahead a show can be scheduled
STATE_MAX = 4 * 1024 * 1024
SIZE_MAX = 64 * 1024 ** 3          # one recording
MARGIN = 1024 ** 3                 # free space on top of what you keep, to start one
GiB = 1024 ** 3
ID_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}\Z")
VIDEO_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}\Z")
HASH_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}\Z")
PROVIDER_RE = re.compile(r"^(src:[0-9a-f]{12}|host:[a-z0-9.-]{1,253})\Z")
VOLATILE = {"tmpfs", "ramfs", "devtmpfs", "proc", "sysfs", "cgroup", "cgroup2", "securityfs", "debugfs", "tracefs",
            "configfs", "devpts", "mqueue", "hugetlbfs", "pstore", "bpf", "efivarfs", "fusectl", "binfmt_misc",
            "autofs", "rpc_pipefs", "nsfs", "overlay", "squashfs"}
TEMPORARY = ("/tmp", "/run", "/dev", "/proc", "/sys", "/dev/shm")
SYSTEM = ("/boot", "/etc", "/usr", "/bin", "/sbin", "/lib", "/lib64", "/opt", "/srv", "/var/lib", "/var/cache", "/var/log", "/root")
PUBLIC = ("id", "kind", "state", "reason", "title", "titles", "desc", "category", "channel", "created", "started",
          "finished", "end", "bytes", "duration", "thumb", "file", "private", "video", "sleepUnprotected", "provider",
          "start", "show", "sub", "ep", "rule", "others", "ids", "rules")


def say(obj):
    print(json.dumps(obj), flush=True)


def xdg(var, rel):
    v = os.environ.get(var, "")
    return v if v.startswith("/") else os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), rel)


def config_home():
    return xdg("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", ".config")


def cache_home():
    return xdg("XDG_CACHE_HOME", ".cache")


def state_dir():
    return os.path.join(config_home(), "om-pg", "dvr")


def thumbs_dir():
    # their own folder: My Videos clears pictures in its own that aren't its videos'
    return os.path.join(cache_home(), "om-pg", "recordings")


def lib_module(name):
    """lib/<name>.py, by its path (never from sys.path)"""
    path = os.path.join(HERE, "lib", name + ".py")
    loader = SourceFileLoader(name, path)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path, loader=loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def relay_module():
    return lib_module("dvrproxy")


def buffer_module():
    return lib_module("dvrbuffer")


# ---- places ----

TEMP_MSG = "temporary"


def unescape(s):
    return re.sub(r"\\([0-7]{3})", lambda m: chr(int(m.group(1), 8)), s)


def mounts(text=None):
    if text is None:
        with open("/proc/self/mountinfo") as f:
            text = f.read()
    out = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        left, _, right = line.partition(" - ")
        f, r = left.split(), right.split()
        if len(f) < 6 or len(r) < 2:
            continue
        out.append({"mount": unescape(f[4]), "fstype": r[0], "source": unescape(r[1]), "ro": "ro" in f[5].split(",")})
    return out


def mount_of(path, table):
    best = None
    for m in table:
        mp = m["mount"]
        if path == mp or path.startswith(mp.rstrip("/") + "/"):
            if best is None or len(mp) >= len(best["mount"]):
                best = m   # the later of two at one place is the one on top
    return best


def volume_of(m, by_uuid=None):
    src = m["source"]
    if src.startswith("/dev/"):
        real = os.path.realpath(src)
        if by_uuid is None:
            by_uuid = {}
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                for name in os.listdir("/dev/disk/by-uuid"):
                    by_uuid[os.path.realpath(os.path.join("/dev/disk/by-uuid", name))] = name
        if real in by_uuid:
            return "uuid:" + by_uuid[real]
        return "dev:" + real
    return "src:" + m["fstype"] + ":" + src


def under(path, top):
    return path == top or path.startswith(top.rstrip("/") + "/")


def lsblk_nodes():
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([LSBLK, "-J", "-b", "-o", "NAME,PATH,TYPE,FSTYPE,UUID,LABEL,SIZE,MOUNTPOINTS,RM,HOTPLUG,RO"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout
        tree = json.loads(out).get("blockdevices", [])
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return []
    flat = []

    def yes(v):
        return v is True or v == "1" or v == 1

    def walk(nodes, removable):
        for n in nodes if isinstance(nodes, list) else []:
            if not isinstance(n, dict):
                continue
            rem = removable or yes(n.get("rm")) or yes(n.get("hotplug"))
            flat.append(dict(n, removable=rem))
            walk(n.get("children"), rem)
    walk(tree, False)
    return flat


def check_place(folder, table=None, home=None, own=None):
    """What a folder is, or {"error": code}: missing, relative, hidden, own, system, temporary, readonly"""
    raw = os.path.expanduser(str(folder or ""))
    if not os.path.isabs(raw):
        return {"error": "relative"}
    p = os.path.realpath(raw)
    if not os.path.isdir(p):
        return {"error": "missing"}
    home = os.path.realpath(home or os.path.expanduser("~"))
    if any(c.startswith(".") for c in p.split("/") if c):
        return {"error": "hidden"}
    own = own if own is not None else [config_home(), cache_home(), os.path.join(home, ".local"), HERE]
    if any(under(p, os.path.realpath(d)) for d in own):
        return {"error": "own"}
    if any(under(p, t) for t in TEMPORARY):
        return {"error": "temporary"}
    if p == "/" or any(under(p, s) for s in SYSTEM):
        return {"error": "system"}
    table = table if table is not None else mounts()
    m = mount_of(p, table)
    if not m:
        return {"error": "missing"}
    if m["fstype"] in VOLATILE:
        return {"error": "temporary"}
    if m["ro"] or not os.access(p, os.W_OK | os.X_OK):
        return {"error": "readonly"}
    home_mount = mount_of(home, table)
    system = bool(home_mount) and volume_of(home_mount) == volume_of(m)
    return {"path": p, "mount": m["mount"], "fstype": m["fstype"], "volume": volume_of(m), "system": system}


def drive_facts(m):
    """A mount's label and whether it's a removable drive"""
    real = os.path.realpath(m["source"]) if m["source"].startswith("/dev/") else ""
    for n in lsblk_nodes() if real else []:
        if n.get("path") and os.path.realpath(n["path"]) == real:
            return n.get("label") or "", n.get("removable", False)
    return "", False


def free_of(path):
    try:
        s = os.statvfs(path)
        return s.f_bavail * s.f_frsize
    except OSError:
        return 0


def prepare(folder, make=False):
    raw = os.path.expanduser(str(folder or ""))
    if make and os.path.isabs(raw) and not os.path.lexists(raw) \
            and os.path.dirname(os.path.normpath(raw)) == os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~")):
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.mkdir(raw, 0o755)   # your Videos folder, the first time
    c = check_place(folder)
    if "error" in c:
        return {"ok": False, "error": c["error"]}
    p = c["path"]
    root = p if os.path.basename(p) == ROOT_NAME else os.path.join(p, ROOT_NAME)
    pfd = os.open(os.path.dirname(root), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    try:
        with contextlib.suppress(FileExistsError):
            os.mkdir(os.path.basename(root), 0o700, dir_fd=pfd)
        st = os.lstat(os.path.basename(root), dir_fd=pfd)
        if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode):
            return {"ok": False, "error": "missing"}
        rfd = os.open(os.path.basename(root), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=pfd)
    finally:
        os.close(pfd)
    try:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.fchmod(rfd, 0o700)
        private = stat.S_IMODE(os.fstat(rfd).st_mode) & 0o077 == 0
        try:
            mfd = os.open(MARKER, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600, dir_fd=rfd)
            os.write(mfd, b'{"uberTV": "recordings"}\n')
            os.close(mfd)
        except FileExistsError:
            if not stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(MARKER, dir_fd=rfd).st_mode):
                return {"ok": False, "error": "missing"}
    finally:
        os.close(rfd)
    m = {"mount": c["mount"], "source": "", "fstype": c["fstype"]}
    for t in mounts():
        if t["mount"] == c["mount"]:
            m = t
    label, removable = drive_facts(m)
    place = {"volume": c["volume"], "mount": c["mount"], "rel": os.path.relpath(root, c["mount"]), "fstype": c["fstype"],
             "label": label, "removable": removable, "system": c["system"]}
    return {"ok": True, "place": place, "path": root, "private": private, "free": free_of(root), "size": size_of(root), "system": c["system"]}


def size_of(path):
    try:
        s = os.statvfs(path)
        return s.f_blocks * s.f_frsize
    except OSError:
        return 0


def where(place):
    root, problem = verify(place)
    system = isinstance(place, dict) and place.get("system") is True
    if not root:
        return {"ok": True, "problem": problem or "drive", "path": "", "free": 0, "size": 0, "system": system}
    return {"ok": True, "problem": problem, "path": root, "free": free_of(root), "size": size_of(root), "system": system}


def verify(place, table=None):
    """(the place's folder, problem): problem "" (fine), "readonly" (can play, not record) or "drive" """
    if not isinstance(place, dict) or not all(isinstance(place.get(k), str) for k in ("volume", "mount", "rel")):
        return None, "drive"
    mount = place["mount"]
    root = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(mount, place["rel"]))
    if not mount.startswith("/") or not under(root, mount) or root == mount:
        return None, "drive"
    table = table if table is not None else mounts()
    m = mount_of(root, table)
    if not m or m["mount"] != mount or volume_of(m) != place["volume"] or m["fstype"] in VOLATILE:
        return None, "drive"
    try:
        if os.path.realpath(root) != root or not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(root).st_mode) \
                or not stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(os.path.join(root, MARKER)).st_mode):
            return None, "drive"
    except OSError:
        return None, "drive"
    if m["ro"] or not os.access(root, os.W_OK | os.X_OK):
        return root, "readonly"
    return root, ""


def drives():
    out = []
    for n in lsblk_nodes():
        if not n.get("removable") or not n.get("fstype") or n.get("fstype") in ("swap", "crypto_LUKS", "LVM2_member"):
            continue
        try:
            size = int(n.get("size") or 0)
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            size = 0
        if size <= 0:
            continue   # an empty card reader
        points = [p for p in (n.get("mountpoints") or []) if isinstance(p, str) and p.startswith("/")]
        mount = points[0] if points else ""
        out.append({"device": n.get("path") or "", "label": n.get("label") or "", "uuid": n.get("uuid") or "",
                    "fstype": n.get("fstype"), "size": size, "mount": mount, "free": free_of(mount) if mount else 0,
                    "ro": n.get("ro") is True or n.get("ro") == "1"})
    return out


def mount_drive(device):
    d = next((d for d in drives() if d["device"] == device), None)
    if not d:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "drive"}
    if d["mount"]:
        return {"ok": True, "mount": d["mount"]}
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([UDISKSCTL, "mount", "--no-user-interaction", "-b", device], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "mount"}
    m = re.search(r" at (/.*?)\.?\s*$", r.stdout.strip())
    if r.returncode != 0 or not m:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "mount"}
    return {"ok": True, "mount": m.group(1)}


# ---- the state ----

def ensure_state_dir():
    d = state_dir()
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(d), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with contextlib.suppress(FileExistsError):
        os.mkdir(d, 0o700)
    st = os.lstat(d)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.getuid():
        raise OSError(errno.ENOTDIR, "the DVR's folder isn't a folder of yours")
    return d


@contextlib.contextmanager
def locked():
    d = ensure_state_dir()
    fd = os.open(os.path.join(d, "lock"), os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        yield
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def load():
    path = os.path.join(state_dir(), "state.json")
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {"version": 1, "recordings": {}, "rules": {}}
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
        data = f.read(STATE_MAX + 1)
    try:
        st = json.loads(data) if len(data) <= STATE_MAX else None
    except ValueError:
        st = None
    if not isinstance(st, dict) or not isinstance(st.get("recordings"), dict):
        # unreadable: kept aside (never overwritten), and a fresh start
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.rename(path, path + ".bad-" + str(int(time.time())))
        return {"version": 1, "recordings": {}, "rules": {}}
    st["recordings"] = {k: v for k, v in st["recordings"].items() if ID_RE.match(str(k)) and isinstance(v, dict)}
    rules = st.get("rules") if isinstance(st.get("rules"), dict) else {}
    st["rules"] = {k: v for k, v in rules.items() if ID_RE.match(str(k)) and isinstance(v, dict)}
    return st


def save(st):
    data = json.dumps(st).encode()
    if len(data) > STATE_MAX:
        raise OSError(errno.EFBIG, "too many recordings")
    d = state_dir()
    tmp = os.path.join(d, "state.json.tmp-" + secrets.token_hex(6))
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, data)
        os.fsync(fd)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(d, "state.json"))


def unit_active(rid):
    try:
        return subprocess.run([SYSTEMCTL, "--user", "is-active", "--quiet", UNIT + rid], timeout=10).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return True   # can't tell: leave it


def reconcile(st, now=None, missed=None):
    """A recording whose worker is gone (killed, the computer off) ends as
    what's on disk says: incomplete if anything was recorded, else failed.
    A scheduled one whose time has gone by without the guide starting it
    (logged out, asleep, off) is Missed (added to missed, to be said)"""
    now = now or time.time()
    changed = False
    for rid, r in st["recordings"].items():
        if r.get("state") == "scheduled" and int(r.get("end") or 0) <= now:
            r.update(state="missed", reason="notRunning", finished=int(now))
            if missed is not None:
                missed.append(r)
            changed = True
            continue
        if r.get("state") not in ACTIVE:
            continue
        beat = r.get("beat") or r.get("created") or 0
        if now - beat < 60 or unit_active(rid):
            continue
        root, problem = verify(r.get("place"))
        size = 0
        if root and problem != "drive":
            size = settle(root, r)
        r.pop("source", None)
        r.pop("handoff", None)
        r["state"] = "incomplete" if size else "failed"
        r["reason"] = "stopped" if size else (r.get("reason") or "stopped")
        r["finished"] = now
        changed = True
    return changed


def settle(root, r):
    """The worker's file put in its place, if the worker couldn't (bytes in it)"""
    name = r.get("file") or ""
    if not safe_name(name):
        return 0
    part = part_name(name)
    try:
        dfd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        return 0
    try:
        try:
            st = os.lstat(part, dir_fd=dfd)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            try:
                return os.lstat(name, dir_fd=dfd).st_size
            except OSError:
                return 0
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or st.st_size == 0:
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                os.unlink(part, dir_fd=dfd)
            return 0
        place_file(dfd, part, name)
        return st.st_size
    finally:
        os.close(dfd)


# ---- names ----

def clean(text, limit=90):
    s = re.sub(r'[\x00-\x1f\x7f/\\:*?"<>|]+', " ", str(text or ""))
    s = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", s).strip().lstrip(".").strip()
    b = s.encode()[:limit * 2]
    s = b.decode("utf-8", "ignore")[:limit].strip()
    return s


def safe_name(name):
    return isinstance(name, str) and 0 < len(name) <= 255 and "/" not in name and "\x00" not in name \
        and not name.startswith(".") and name not in (".", "..")


def part_name(name):
    base, ext = os.path.splitext(name)
    return base + ".part" + ext


def file_name(title, channel, when, ext, taken):
    stamp = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H.%M", time.localtime(when))
    parts = [p for p in (clean(title), clean(channel, 60)) if p]
    if len(parts) == 2 and parts[0] == parts[1]:
        parts = parts[:1]
    base = " – ".join(parts + [stamp]) or stamp
    name = base + ext
    n = 2
    while taken(name) or taken(part_name(name)):
        name = f"{base} ({n}){ext}"
        n += 1
    return name


def place_file(dfd, src, dst):
    """src renamed to dst in one folder, never over a file already there"""
    try:
        os.link(src, dst, src_dir_fd=dfd, dst_dir_fd=dfd, follow_symlinks=False)
        os.unlink(src, dir_fd=dfd)
    except FileExistsError:
        raise
    except OSError:
        # a drive without hard links (FAT, exFAT)
        try:
            os.lstat(dst, dir_fd=dfd)
            raise FileExistsError(dst)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            os.rename(src, dst, src_dir_fd=dfd, dst_dir_fd=dfd)


# ---- starting, stopping ----

def text_of(v, limit):
    return re.sub(r"[\x00-\x08\x0b-\x1f\x7f]", "", v)[:limit] if isinstance(v, str) else ""


def job_from(raw, now):
    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
        return None, "job"
    kind = raw.get("kind")
    if kind not in KINDS:
        return None, "job"
    ch = raw.get("channel") if isinstance(raw.get("channel"), dict) else {}
    h = ch.get("hash") if isinstance(ch.get("hash"), str) and HASH_RE.match(ch.get("hash")) else ""
    try:
        number = int(ch.get("number") or 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        number = 0
    job = {"kind": kind, "channel": {"name": text_of(ch.get("name"), 200), "number": number, "hash": h},
           "title": text_of(raw.get("title"), 300), "desc": text_of(raw.get("desc"), 2000),
           "category": text_of(raw.get("category"), 100), "private": raw.get("private") is True,
           "provider": raw.get("provider") if isinstance(raw.get("provider"), str) and PROVIDER_RE.match(raw.get("provider")) else ""}
    q = raw.get("quality", 1080)
    job["quality"] = q if q in QUALITIES else 1080
    try:
        keep = int(raw.get("keepFree", 5 * GiB))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None, "job"
    job["keepFree"] = max(GiB, min(100 * GiB, keep))
    if kind == "iptv":
        url = raw.get("url")
        if not isinstance(url, str) or len(url) > 4096 or not re.match(r"^https?://[^\s]+\Z", url):
            return None, "job"
        job["source"] = {"url": url}
    else:
        vid = raw.get("video")
        if not isinstance(vid, str) or not VIDEO_RE.match(vid):
            return None, "job"
        job["source"] = {"video": vid}
        job["video"] = vid
    if kind == "youtube-video":
        job["end"] = 0
    else:
        try:
            end = int(raw.get("end"))
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            return None, "job"
        if end <= now or end > now + MAX_HOURS * 3600:
            return None, "job"
        job["end"] = end
    if kind == "iptv":
        # a listed show recorded now (a series' episode among them): its episode, its series, its times
        job["sub"], job["ep"] = text_of(raw.get("sub"), 200), text_of(raw.get("ep"), 60)
        job["rule"] = raw.get("rule") if isinstance(raw.get("rule"), str) and ID_RE.match(raw.get("rule")) else ""
        show = raw.get("show") if isinstance(raw.get("show"), dict) else {}
        try:
            a, b = int(show.get("start")), int(show.get("end"))
            if a < b <= a + MAX_HOURS * 3600:
                job["show"] = {"start": a, "end": b}
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            pass
    job["place"] = raw.get("place")
    return job, ""


def names_of(recs):
    return [r.get("title") or r.get("channel", {}).get("name") or "a recording" if not r.get("private") else "a recording" for r in recs]


# ---- scheduled ----

def fold(text):
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", str(text or "")).strip().casefold()


def identity(r):
    """A show's identity on its channel: its title with its episode number,
    else with its episode's title, else when it starts (so a series doesn't
    record one episode twice, a rerun included; two shows' S1E2 aren't one)"""
    if fold(r.get("ep")):
        return "ep:" + fold(r.get("title")) + "|" + fold(r.get("ep"))
    if fold(r.get("sub")):
        return "sub:" + fold(r.get("title")) + "|" + fold(r.get("sub"))
    show = r.get("show") if isinstance(r.get("show"), dict) else {}
    return "at:%d" % int(show.get("start") or r.get("start") or 0)


def identities(r):
    """Every show a recording holds (episodes back to back are joined into
    one recording): their identities"""
    ids = [k for k in (r.get("ids") or []) if isinstance(k, str)][:MAX_IDS]
    return ids or [identity(r)]


def rules_of(r):
    """Every series a recording's shows are of"""
    held = [k for k in (r.get("rules") or []) if isinstance(k, str) and ID_RE.match(k)]
    if r.get("rule") and r["rule"] not in held:
        held.insert(0, r["rule"])
    return held[:MAX_RULES_HELD]


def merge_shows(into, r):
    """A show joined into a running recording: its identity and its series
    kept with it (so its rerun isn't recorded), every one a 12-hour
    recording can hold"""
    ids = identities(into)
    for k in identities(r):
        if k not in ids:
            ids.append(k)
    into["ids"] = ids[-MAX_IDS:]
    held = rules_of(into)
    for k in rules_of(r):
        if k not in held:
            held.append(k)
    if held:
        into["rules"] = held[:MAX_RULES_HELD]
        into.setdefault("rule", held[0])


def stream_key(r):
    """What takes one stream: a channel (shows back to back on it are one;
    an IPTV channel by its provider and name, as its address may turn), or a
    video being saved, on its own"""
    ch = r.get("channel", {})
    if r.get("kind") == "youtube-video":
        return r.get("id")
    if r.get("kind") == "iptv" and r.get("provider") and fold(ch.get("name")):
        return "ch:" + r["provider"] + "|" + fold(ch.get("name"))
    return ch.get("hash") or r.get("id")


def channel_of(raw):
    ch = raw.get("channel") if isinstance(raw.get("channel"), dict) else {}
    h = ch.get("hash") if isinstance(ch.get("hash"), str) and HASH_RE.match(ch.get("hash")) else ""
    try:
        number = int(ch.get("number") or 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        number = 0
    return {"name": text_of(ch.get("name"), 200), "number": number, "hash": h}


def provider_of(raw):
    p = raw.get("provider")
    return p if isinstance(p, str) and PROVIDER_RE.match(p) else ""


def slot_from(raw, now):
    """A show to record later (IPTV, from its listings): its times and its
    padding, checked; None if it can't be one"""
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or raw.get("kind") != "iptv":
        return None
    ch = channel_of(raw)
    title = text_of(raw.get("title"), 300).strip()
    if not ch["hash"] or not title:
        return None
    try:
        a, b = int(raw.get("showStart")), int(raw.get("showEnd"))
        early, late = int(raw.get("early", 60)), int(raw.get("late", 120))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not (0 <= early <= 600 and 0 <= late <= 900 and a + MIN_SHOW <= b <= a + MAX_HOURS * 3600):
        return None
    start, end = a - early, min(b + late, a - early + MAX_HOURS * 3600)
    if end <= now or start > now + MAX_AHEAD:
        return None
    rule = raw.get("rule") if isinstance(raw.get("rule"), str) and ID_RE.match(raw.get("rule")) else ""
    return {"kind": "iptv", "channel": ch, "title": title, "sub": text_of(raw.get("sub"), 200), "ep": text_of(raw.get("ep"), 60),
            "desc": text_of(raw.get("desc"), 2000), "category": text_of(raw.get("category"), 100), "private": raw.get("private") is True,
            "provider": provider_of(raw), "show": {"start": a, "end": b}, "start": start, "end": end, "rule": rule}


def span(r, now):
    """When one takes a stream: a waiting one its window, a running one from
    now to its stop (a video being saved: an hour, as a guess)"""
    if r.get("state") in WAITING:
        return max(int(r.get("start") or 0), now), int(r.get("end") or 0)
    return now, int(r.get("end") or 0) or now + 3600


def cap_of(st):
    """How many may record at once"""
    return st.get("atOnce") if st.get("atOnce") in AT_ONCE else 2


def recheck(st, now):
    """Which waiting ones fit: at most cap_of(st) streams at any moment, two
    shows back to back on one channel being one stream. The ones scheduled
    first keep their place; a later one that would be one too many waits as
    a Conflict, naming the others, and is Scheduled again once one goes.
    True if anything changed"""
    recs = st["recordings"]
    fixed = [r for r in recs.values() if r.get("state") in ACTIVE]
    waiting = sorted((r for r in recs.values() if r.get("state") in WAITING and int(r.get("end") or 0) > now),
                     key=lambda r: (r.get("seq") or 0, r.get("created") or 0, r.get("id") or ""))
    chosen = []
    changed = False
    for r in waiting:
        a, b = span(r, now)
        key = stream_key(r)
        cover = []
        for o in fixed + chosen:
            oa, ob = span(o, now)
            if oa < b and ob > a and stream_key(o) != key:
                cover.append((oa, ob, o))
        peak = 0
        for t in [a] + [oa for oa, ob, o in cover if oa > a]:
            peak = max(peak, len({stream_key(o) for oa, ob, o in cover if oa <= t < ob}))
        was = (r.get("state"), r.get("others"))
        if peak >= cap_of(st):
            # the others by their ids, once a stream (never their names: a
            # channel locked later would still be named); the guide names
            # them as the lock is when it says so
            streams = {}
            for oa, ob, o in sorted(cover, key=lambda c: c[0]):
                streams.setdefault(stream_key(o), o["id"])
            r.update(state="conflict", reason="conflict", others=list(streams.values())[:3])
        else:
            r.update(state="scheduled", reason="")
            r.pop("others", None)
            chosen.append(r)
        changed = changed or was != (r.get("state"), r.get("others"))
    return changed


def schedule(raw, now=None):
    """Shows to record later: each Scheduled (or a Conflict); one already
    scheduled (or, for a series, an episode already recorded) isn't added
    twice"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    items = raw.get("slots") if isinstance(raw, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(items, list) or not items or len(items) > 100:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        reconcile(st, now)
        recs = st["recordings"]
        out = []
        for item in items:
            slot = slot_from(item, now)
            if not slot:
                out.append({"ok": False, "error": "job"})
                continue
            h, key = slot["channel"]["hash"], identity(slot)
            if slot["rule"]:
                rule = st["rules"].get(slot["rule"])
                if not rule:
                    out.append({"ok": False, "error": "rule"})   # the series was stopped meanwhile
                    continue
                if key in rule.get("skip", []):
                    out.append({"ok": True, "skipped": True})
                    continue
                # by its series (its channel's address may have changed since) or its channel, every show a recording holds
                dup = next((r for r in recs.values() if (r.get("channel", {}).get("hash") == h or slot["rule"] in rules_of(r))
                            and r.get("state") not in ("failed", "missed") and not (r.get("state") == "conflict" and int(r.get("end") or 0) <= now)
                            and key in identities(r)), None)
            else:
                dup = next((r for r in recs.values() if r.get("channel", {}).get("hash") == h and r.get("state") in WAITING + ACTIVE
                            and (r.get("show") or {}).get("start") == slot["show"]["start"]), None)
            if dup:
                out.append({"ok": True, "id": dup["id"], "already": True})
                continue
            if len(recs) >= MAX_RECORDINGS:
                out.append({"ok": False, "error": "full"})
                continue
            rid = secrets.token_hex(8)
            st["seq"] = int(st.get("seq") or 0) + 1   # the order they were scheduled in (who keeps their place)
            recs[rid] = dict(slot, id=rid, state="scheduled", reason="", created=now, seq=st["seq"], titles=[slot["title"]], bytes=0, ids=[key])
            out.append({"ok": True, "id": rid})
        recheck(st, now)
        save(st)
        for o in out:
            r = recs.get(o.get("id") or "")
            if r:
                o.update(state=r["state"], others=r.get("others", []))
    return {"ok": True, "slots": out}


def limit(n, now=None):
    """How many may record at once, from the guide's setting: one running
    goes on; the scheduled ones are checked again against it"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    if n not in AT_ONCE:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        st["atOnce"] = n
        recheck(st, now)
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True, "atOnce": n}


def tag(raw, now=None):
    """Record every episode on a show that's recording already: the show
    joined to that recording, in one go: its stop moved to the show's end
    (plus late, within its 12 hours), its title, episode and series kept with
    it. One that's ended ("ended") or can't run that long ("long") isn't
    tagged: the guide records the show itself"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not isinstance(raw.get("id"), str) or not ID_RE.match(raw["id"]):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    rule = raw.get("rule") if isinstance(raw.get("rule"), str) and ID_RE.match(raw.get("rule")) else ""
    show = raw.get("show") if isinstance(raw.get("show"), dict) else {}
    try:
        a, b = int(show.get("start")), int(show.get("end"))
        late = int(raw.get("late", 120))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    if not (a + MIN_SHOW <= b <= a + MAX_HOURS * 3600 and 0 <= late <= 900 and b > now):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    url = raw.get("url")
    if url is not None and (not isinstance(url, str) or len(url) > 4096 or not re.match(r"^https?://[^\s]+\Z", url)):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    one = {"title": text_of(raw.get("title"), 300), "sub": text_of(raw.get("sub"), 200), "ep": text_of(raw.get("ep"), 60),
           "show": {"start": a, "end": b}, "rule": rule}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(raw["id"])
        if not r:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if r.get("state") not in ACTIVE or r.get("stop"):
            return {"ok": False, "error": "ended"}
        if rule and rule not in st["rules"]:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "rule"}
        follow(r, url)                         # its channel's address as the guide has it now
        latest = latest_of(r, now)
        if one["title"] and one["title"] not in r.get("titles", []):
            r["titles"] = (r.get("titles") or [])[:4] + [one["title"]]
        if b + late <= latest:
            r["end"] = max(int(r.get("end") or 0), b + late)
            merge_shows(r, one)
            save(st)
            return {"ok": True, "id": r["id"], "end": r["end"]}
        # past its 12 hours: it records to its end, and a continuation from
        # there holds the show (its worker starts it at once then)
        if len(st["recordings"]) >= MAX_RECORDINGS:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "full"}
        cid = continuation(st, r, one, b + late, now)
        save(st)
        return {"ok": True, "id": r["id"], "end": r["end"], "continued": cid}


def follow_cmd(raw):
    """A running recording's channel at a new address (the guide saw its
    playlist turn the link): it moves to it, the same file going on"""
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not isinstance(raw.get("id"), str) or not ID_RE.match(raw["id"]):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    url = raw.get("url")
    if not isinstance(url, str) or len(url) > 4096 or not re.match(r"^https?://[^\s]+\Z", url):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(raw["id"])
        if not r or r.get("state") not in ACTIVE or r.get("kind") != "iptv":
            return {"ok": False, "error": "notRecording"}
        follow(r, url)
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True}


def clear(now=None):
    """Recordings turned off: every scheduled one off the list, at once (the
    series rules stay, and schedule again once it's back on)"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    with locked():
        st = load()
        recs = st["recordings"]
        gone = [k for k, r in recs.items() if r.get("state") in WAITING]
        for k in gone:
            del recs[k]
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True, "cleared": len(gone)}


def series_add(raw, now=None):
    """Record every episode: a rule, a channel and a title (the guide
    schedules its episodes as its listings come)"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    ch, title = channel_of(raw), text_of(raw.get("title"), 300).strip()
    if not ch["hash"] or not title:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        rules = st["rules"]
        provider = provider_of(raw)
        # the same series: its channel by its address, or (its address
        # changed since: a playlist that turns its links) by its name from the
        # same provider, its address then brought up to date
        had = next((x for x in rules.values() if fold(x.get("title")) == fold(title) and (x.get("channel", {}).get("hash") == ch["hash"]
                    or (provider and x.get("provider") == provider and fold(x.get("channel", {}).get("name")) == fold(ch["name"])))), None)
        if had:
            if had.get("channel", {}).get("hash") != ch["hash"]:
                had["channel"] = ch
                save(st)
            return {"ok": True, "id": had["id"], "already": True}
        if len(rules) >= MAX_RULES:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "full"}
        rid = secrets.token_hex(8)
        rules[rid] = {"id": rid, "channel": ch, "title": title, "provider": provider, "private": raw.get("private") is True,
                      "created": now, "skip": []}
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True, "id": rid}


def series_remove(rid, now=None):
    """Stops recording a series: its rule, and its shows not started yet
    (what it recorded stays)"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    with locked():
        st = load()
        if rid not in st["rules"]:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        del st["rules"][rid]
        recs = st["recordings"]
        gone = [k for k, r in recs.items() if r.get("rule") == rid and r.get("state") in WAITING]
        for k in gone:
            del recs[k]
        recheck(st, now)
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True, "cancelled": len(gone)}


def cancel(rid, now=None):
    """A scheduled one cancelled (a series' episode isn't scheduled again);
    a missed one taken off the list; a running one stops"""
    now = int(now or time.time())
    with locked():
        st = load()
        recs = st["recordings"]
        r = recs.get(rid)
        if not r:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if r.get("state") in ACTIVE:
            r["stop"] = True
            save(st)
            return {"ok": True, "stopping": True}
        if r.get("state") not in WAITING + ("missed",):
            return {"ok": False, "error": "notScheduled"}
        rule = st["rules"].get(r.get("rule") or "")
        if rule and r.get("state") in WAITING:
            key = identity(r)
            rule["skip"] = ([k for k in rule.get("skip", []) if k != key] + [key])[-MAX_SKIP:]
        del recs[rid]
        recheck(st, now)
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True}


def start(raw, now=None):
    now = int(now or time.time())
    if isinstance(raw, dict) and "slot" in raw:
        return claim(raw, now)
    job, bad = job_from(raw, now)
    if bad:
        return {"ok": False, "error": bad}
    with locked():
        st = load()
        if reconcile(st, now):
            save(st)
        recs = st["recordings"]
        active = [r for r in recs.values() if r.get("state") in ACTIVE]
        if job["kind"] != "youtube-video" and job["channel"]["hash"]:
            # the same stream: its channel's address hashed, or (IPTV) its provider and name, as its address may have turned
            same = [r for r in active if r.get("kind") == job["kind"] and (r.get("channel", {}).get("hash") == job["channel"]["hash"]
                                                                          or (job["kind"] == "iptv" and stream_key(r) == stream_key(job)))]
            if same:
                # back to back on one channel: one recording, its stop later (one stream)
                r = same[0]
                if job["kind"] == "iptv":
                    follow(r, job["source"]["url"])   # the address as the guide has it now
                if job["title"] and job["title"] not in r.get("titles", []):
                    r["titles"] = (r.get("titles") or [])[:4] + [job["title"]]
                if job["end"] > latest_of(r, now) and job["kind"] == "iptv":
                    # past its 12 hours: a continuation from its end holds the show
                    if len(recs) >= MAX_RECORDINGS:
                        return {"ok": False, "error": "full"}
                    cid = continuation(st, r, job, job["end"], now)
                    save(st)
                    return {"ok": True, "id": r["id"], "joined": True, "end": r["end"], "continued": cid}
                r["end"] = min(max(r.get("end", 0), job["end"]), latest_of(r, now))
                if job.get("show"):
                    merge_shows(r, job)
                save(st)
                return {"ok": True, "id": r["id"], "joined": True, "end": r["end"]}
        if job["kind"] == "youtube-video":
            had = next((r for r in recs.values() if r.get("video") == job["video"] and r.get("kind") == "youtube-video"
                        and r.get("state") in ACTIVE + ("done",)), None)
            if had:
                return {"ok": True, "id": had["id"], "already": True}
        if len(active) >= cap_of(st):
            return {"ok": False, "error": "cap", "recording": names_of(active)}
        if len(recs) >= MAX_RECORDINGS:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "full"}
        root, problem = verify(job["place"])
        if problem:
            return {"ok": False, "error": problem}
        free = free_of(root)
        if free < job["keepFree"] + MARGIN:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "space", "free": free}
        rid = secrets.token_hex(8)
        ext = ".mkv" if job["kind"] == "youtube-video" else ".ts"
        name = file_name(job["title"] or job["channel"]["name"], job["channel"]["name"], now, ext,
                         lambda n: os.path.lexists(os.path.join(root, n)) or any(r.get("file") == n for r in recs.values()))
        entry = dict(job, id=rid, state="starting", reason="", created=now, start=now, file=name,
                     titles=[job["title"]] if job["title"] else [], bytes=0)
        if job.get("show"):
            entry["ids"] = [identity(job)]
        recs[rid] = entry
        save(st)
    return launch(rid, job["end"])


def claim(raw, now):
    """A scheduled one that's due, started: claimed under the lock (only a
    Scheduled one starts, and once), with its channel's address as the guide
    has it now ("gone": it hasn't); its title and times are the schedule's.
    Joins a recording already on that channel (back to back: one stream)"""
    rid = raw.get("slot")
    if not isinstance(rid, str) or not ID_RE.match(rid):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    gone = raw.get("gone") is True
    url = raw.get("url")
    if not gone and (not isinstance(url, str) or len(url) > 4096 or not re.match(r"^https?://[^\s]+\Z", url)):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    q = raw.get("quality", 1080)
    q = q if q in QUALITIES else 1080
    try:
        keep = max(GiB, min(100 * GiB, int(raw.get("keepFree", 5 * GiB))))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return {"ok": False, "error": "job"}
    said, missed, result = None, [], None
    with locked():
        st = load()
        reconcile(st, now, missed)
        recs = st["recordings"]
        r = recs.get(rid)
        if not r or r.get("state") != "scheduled":
            result = {"ok": False, "error": "notScheduled", "state": (r or {}).get("state", "")}
        elif now < int(r.get("start") or 0) - 60:
            result = {"ok": False, "error": "early"}
        elif (recs.get(r.get("after") or "") or {}).get("state") in ACTIVE:
            # a continuation: it starts once the recording before it has ended (that recording's worker starts it)
            result = {"ok": False, "error": "early"}
        elif gone:
            r.update(state="failed", reason="gone", finished=now)
            said, result = dict(r), {"ok": False, "error": "gone"}
        else:
            active = [x for x in recs.values() if x.get("state") in ACTIVE]
            # the same stream, as the planning has it (stream_key: by provider and name, its address may have
            # turned), its channel's address hashed as scheduled, or the address as the guide has it now; the
            # recording running goes on, its stop later
            same = next((x for x in active if x.get("kind") == "iptv" and (x.get("channel", {}).get("hash") == r["channel"]["hash"]
                                                                          or (x.get("source") or {}).get("url") == url
                                                                          or stream_key(x) == stream_key(r))), None)
            latest = latest_of(same, now) if same else 0
            if same:
                follow(same, url)              # the address as the guide has it now, whichever way it goes on
            if same and int(r["end"]) > latest:
                # past that recording's 12 hours: a continuation, from its end (its worker starts it then);
                # the show is this one's, not the one that can't hold it
                r["start"], r["after"] = latest, same["id"]
                same.setdefault("then", rid)
                result = {"ok": False, "error": "early", "after": same["id"]}
            elif same:
                same["end"] = max(int(same.get("end") or 0), int(r["end"]))
                if r["title"] not in same.get("titles", []):
                    same["titles"] = (same.get("titles") or [])[:4] + [r["title"]]
                merge_shows(same, r)
                del recs[rid]
                result = {"ok": True, "id": same["id"], "joined": True, "end": same["end"]}
            elif len(active) >= cap_of(st):
                r.update(state="conflict", reason="conflict", others=[x["id"] for x in active][:3])
                said, result = dict(r), {"ok": False, "error": "cap", "recording": names_of(active)}
            else:
                root, problem = verify(raw.get("place"))
                if not problem and free_of(root) < keep + MARGIN:
                    problem = "space"
                if problem:
                    r.update(state="failed", reason=problem, finished=now)
                    said, result = dict(r), {"ok": False, "error": problem}
                else:
                    name = file_name(r["title"], r["channel"]["name"], now, ".ts",
                                     lambda n: os.path.lexists(os.path.join(root, n)) or any(x.get("file") == n for x in recs.values()))
                    r.update(state="starting", reason="", start=now, file=name, source={"url": url}, place=raw.get("place"),
                             keepFree=keep, quality=q, bytes=0)
                    r.pop("others", None)
        recheck(st, now)
        save(st)
        end = int(r.get("end") or 0) if r else 0
    for m in missed:
        notify(m)
    notify(said)
    return result if result is not None else launch(rid, end)


def seg_start(r, now=None):
    """When a running recording began (its 12 hours run from then): a
    scheduled one when it was claimed, not when it was scheduled"""
    return int(r.get("start") or r.get("created") or now or time.time())


def latest_of(r, now=None):
    return seg_start(r, now) + MAX_HOURS * 3600


def follow(r, url):
    """A running IPTV recording told its channel's address now: it moves to
    it (handoff), and goes by that address hashed from now on"""
    if r.get("kind") != "iptv" or not url:
        return
    handoff(r, url)
    r.setdefault("channel", {})["hash"] = hashlib.sha256(url.encode("utf-8", "surrogatepass")).hexdigest()


def continuation(st, prev, one, end, now):
    """A show past prev's 12 hours: prev records to its end, and this entry,
    from there, holds the show (prev's worker starts it then; the checker if
    it can't)"""
    latest = latest_of(prev, now)
    prev["end"] = latest
    cid = secrets.token_hex(8)
    st["seq"] = int(st.get("seq") or 0) + 1
    st["recordings"][cid] = {"id": cid, "kind": "iptv", "state": "scheduled", "reason": "", "created": now, "seq": st["seq"],
                             "channel": dict(prev.get("channel") or {}), "provider": prev.get("provider", ""), "private": prev.get("private") is True,
                             "title": one.get("title", ""), "titles": [one["title"]] if one.get("title") else [], "sub": one.get("sub", ""),
                             "ep": one.get("ep", ""), "desc": one.get("desc", ""), "category": prev.get("category", ""), "show": one.get("show"),
                             "start": latest, "end": min(int(end), latest + MAX_HOURS * 3600), "rule": one.get("rule", ""),
                             "ids": [identity(one)] if one.get("show") else [], "after": prev["id"], "bytes": 0}
    prev.setdefault("then", cid)
    return cid


def handoff(r, url):
    """A running IPTV recording told its channel's address now (a playlist
    that turned its links): its worker moves to it, the same file going on"""
    if r.get("kind") != "iptv" or not url or (r.get("source") or {}).get("url") == url:
        return
    gen = int((r.get("handoff") or {}).get("gen") or 0) + 1
    r["handoff"] = {"url": url, "gen": gen}


def launch(rid, end):
    """The recording's own service, started: its worker does the rest"""
    argv = [SYSTEMD_RUN, "--user", "--quiet", "--collect", "--unit=" + UNIT + rid, "--service-type=exec",
            "--expand-environment=no", "--description=Uber TV recording", "-p", "MemoryMax=768M", "-p", "CPUWeight=20", "-p", "KillMode=mixed",
            "-p", "RuntimeMaxSec=%d" % ((MAX_HOURS + 1) * 3600)]
    for var in ("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", "XDG_CACHE_HOME"):
        if os.environ.get(var, "").startswith("/"):
            argv.append("--setenv=%s=%s" % (var, os.environ[var]))
    argv += ["--", PYTHON, "-I", os.path.realpath(__file__), "run", rid]
    try:
        ok = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, timeout=30).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        ok = False
    if not ok:
        finish(rid, "failed", "service")
        return {"ok": False, "error": "service"}
    return {"ok": True, "id": rid, "end": end}


def stop(rid):
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(rid)
        if not r:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if r.get("state") not in ACTIVE:
            return {"ok": True}
        r["stop"] = True
        save(st)
    return {"ok": True}


def until(rid, end, now=None):
    now = int(now or time.time())
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(rid)
        if not r:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if r.get("state") not in ACTIVE or r.get("kind") == "youtube-video":
            return {"ok": False, "error": "notRecording"}
        latest = latest_of(r, now)
        if end < now + 30 or end > latest:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "time", "latest": latest}
        r["end"] = int(end)
        save(st)
        return {"ok": True, "end": r["end"]}


def listing():
    now = int(time.time())
    missed = []
    with locked():
        st = load()
        if reconcile(st, now, missed) | recheck(st, now):
            save(st)
    for m in missed:
        notify(m)
    table = mounts()
    seen = {}
    out = []
    for r in sorted(st["recordings"].values(), key=lambda r: -(r.get("created") or 0)):
        d = {k: r.get(k) for k in PUBLIC if k in r}
        place = r.get("place") if isinstance(r.get("place"), dict) else {}
        key = (place.get("volume"), place.get("mount"), place.get("rel"))
        if key not in seen:
            seen[key] = verify(place, table)
        root, problem = seen[key]
        d["present"] = root is not None
        d["placeLabel"] = place.get("label") or ""
        d["path"] = os.path.join(root, r["file"]) if root and r.get("state") in ("done", "incomplete") and safe_name(r.get("file")) else ""
        out.append(d)
    rules = [{k: x.get(k) for k in ("id", "channel", "title", "private", "provider", "created")}
             for x in sorted(st["rules"].values(), key=lambda x: x.get("created") or 0)]
    return {"ok": True, "recordings": out, "rules": rules}


def remove(rid):
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(rid)
        if not r:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if r.get("state") in ACTIVE:
            r["stop"] = True
            save(st)
    if r.get("state") in ACTIVE:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            subprocess.run([SYSTEMCTL, "--user", "stop", UNIT + rid], capture_output=True, timeout=40)
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(rid)
        if not r:
            return {"ok": True}
        root, problem = verify(r.get("place"))
        gone = False
        name = r.get("file") or ""
        if root and problem != "drive" and safe_name(name):
            dfd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
            try:
                for n in (name, part_name(name), os.path.splitext(name)[0] + ".json"):
                    with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
                        if stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(n, dir_fd=dfd).st_mode):
                            os.unlink(n, dir_fd=dfd)
                drop_work(dfd, rid)
                gone = True
            finally:
                os.close(dfd)
        thumb = os.path.join(thumbs_dir(), "rec-%s.jpg" % rid)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.unlink(thumb)
        del st["recordings"][rid]
        save(st)
        return {"ok": True, "forgotten": not gone}


def drop_work(dfd, rid):
    work = ".work-" + rid
    try:
        wfd = os.open(work, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dfd)
    except OSError:
        return
    try:
        for n in os.listdir(wfd):
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                if not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(n, dir_fd=wfd).st_mode):
                    os.unlink(n, dir_fd=wfd)
    finally:
        os.close(wfd)
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.rmdir(work, dir_fd=dfd)


def finish(rid, state, reason, extra=None):
    with locked():
        st = load()
        r = st["recordings"].get(rid)
        if not r:
            return None
        r.pop("source", None)
        r.pop("handoff", None)
        r.pop("stop", None)
        r["state"] = state
        r["reason"] = reason
        r["finished"] = int(time.time())
        r.update(extra or {})
        save(st)
        return dict(r)


# ---- the recording itself ----

def classify(err):
    e = err.lower()
    if re.search(r"\b(401|403|404|429|451|458|509)\b|forbidden|unauthorized|not found|too many", e):
        return "refused"
    if re.search(r"timed out|connection refused|unreachable|name or service|resolve|reset by peer|i/o error", e):
        return "network"
    if "invalid data" in e or "could not find codec" in e:
        return "unreadable"
    return "stopped"


class Tail(threading.Thread):
    """The last few KB a process said on stderr"""

    def __init__(self, pipe):
        super().__init__(daemon=True)
        self.pipe = pipe
        self.text = ""

    def run(self):
        for chunk in iter(lambda: self.pipe.read(1024), b""):
            self.text = (self.text + chunk.decode("utf-8", "replace"))[-8192:]


def inhibit():
    try:
        p = subprocess.Popen([INHIBIT, "--what=sleep", "--who=Uber TV", "--why=Recording TV", "--mode=block", SLEEP, "infinity"],
                             stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True)
    except OSError:
        return None
    time.sleep(0.4)
    if p.poll() is not None:
        return None
    return p


def youtube_manifest(video):
    out = subprocess.run([YTDLP, "--ignore-config", "--no-plugin-dirs", "--no-playlist", "--no-warnings", "-J", "--",
                          "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=" + video], capture_output=True, timeout=120)
    info = json.loads(out.stdout[:32 * 1024 * 1024] or b"{}")
    if not isinstance(info, dict):
        raise LookupError("not live")
    for f in info.get("formats") or []:
        if str(f.get("protocol", "")).startswith("m3u8") and isinstance(f.get("manifest_url"), str):
            return f["manifest_url"]
    raise LookupError("no live stream")


def ffmpeg_argv(url):
    """ffmpeg copying a stream from the relay (http and https only) to its stdout, as MPEG-TS"""
    return [FFMPEG, "-nostdin", "-hide_banner", "-loglevel", "error",
            "-protocol_whitelist", "http,https,tcp,tls,crypto",
            "-reconnect", "1", "-reconnect_streamed", "1", "-reconnect_on_network_error", "1",
            "-reconnect_delay_max", "10", "-rw_timeout", "20000000",
            "-i", url, "-map", "0:v:0?", "-map", "0:a:0?", "-c", "copy", "-f", "mpegts", "pipe:1"]


class Worker:
    def __init__(self, rid):
        self.rid = rid
        self.stopping = False
        self.unprotected = False
        self.url = ""                  # the address it's recording from now (IPTV)
        self.handoff_gen = 0           # the last move to a new address it made
        for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
            signal.signal(s, self.on_signal)

    def on_signal(self, *args):
        self.stopping = True

    def read(self):
        with locked():
            return load()["recordings"].get(self.rid)

    def beat(self, **changes):
        with locked():
            st = load()
            r = st["recordings"].get(self.rid)
            if not r:
                return None
            r.update(changes, beat=int(time.time()))
            save(st)
            return dict(r)

    def run(self):
        os.umask(0o077)   # what it and its tools write (yt-dlp's video too) is yours alone
        with locked():
            st = load()
            r = st["recordings"].get(self.rid)
            if not r or r.get("state") != "starting":
                return
            r["beat"] = int(time.time())
            save(st)
        root, problem = verify(r.get("place"))
        if problem:
            done = finish(self.rid, "failed", problem)
            notify(done)
            return
        sleep_guard = inhibit()
        if not sleep_guard:
            self.beat(sleepUnprotected=True)   # said while it records, not after
        self.unprotected = not sleep_guard
        dfd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
        try:
            if r["kind"] == "youtube-video":
                state, reason, extra = self.save_video(r, root, dfd)
            else:
                state, reason, extra = self.record_live(r, root, dfd)
        except Exception:
            # whatever was recorded before it went wrong is kept
            size = settle(root, r)
            state, reason, extra = ("incomplete" if size else "failed"), "stopped", {"bytes": size} if size else {}
        finally:
            os.close(dfd)
            if sleep_guard:
                with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                    os.killpg(sleep_guard.pid, signal.SIGTERM)
        if state is None:
            # stopped before anything was kept (a video save cancelled): gone
            with locked():
                st = load()
                st["recordings"].pop(self.rid, None)
                save(st)
            return
        # said done (or how it ended) at once; its length and picture follow
        done = finish(self.rid, state, reason, extra)
        # a continuation waiting (a show past its 12 hours): started now,
        # from the address it was recording, before its length and picture
        nxt = (done or {}).get("then")
        if nxt and state in ("done", "incomplete") and self.url and time.time() >= int(done.get("end") or 0) - 10:
            with contextlib.suppress(Exception):
                claim({"slot": nxt, "url": self.url, "place": r.get("place"), "keepFree": r.get("keepFree", 5 * GiB),
                       "quality": r.get("quality", 1080)}, int(time.time()))
        if done and state in ("done", "incomplete"):
            path = os.path.join(root, done["file"])
            more = {"duration": duration_of(path), "thumb": thumb_of(path, self.rid)}
            with locked():
                st = load()
                if self.rid in st["recordings"]:
                    st["recordings"][self.rid].update(more)
                    save(st)
            done.update(more)
        notify(done)

    def should_stop(self, r, root, size, keep):
        """("done" | "incomplete" | None, reason)"""
        if self.stopping or not r or r.get("stop"):
            return "done", ""
        if r.get("end") and time.time() >= r["end"]:
            return "done", ""
        if free_of(root) < keep:
            return "incomplete", "space"
        if size > SIZE_MAX:
            return "incomplete", "size"
        return None, ""

    def record_live(self, r, root, dfd):
        name = r["file"]
        part = part_name(name)
        fd = os.open(part, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600, dir_fd=dfd)
        relay = None
        proc = None
        tail = None
        outcome, reason = None, ""
        try:
            if r["kind"] == "iptv":
                upstream, height = r["source"]["url"], 1080
            else:
                try:
                    upstream, height = youtube_manifest(r["source"]["video"]), r.get("quality", 1080)
                except (OSError, ValueError, LookupError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
                    os.close(fd)
                    fd = None
                    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                        os.unlink(part, dir_fd=dfd)
                    return "failed", "offline", {}
            self.url = upstream if r["kind"] == "iptv" else ""
            relay, proc, tail = self.open_input(upstream, height, fd)
            last_beat = 0
            acknowledged = False
            while True:
                try:
                    proc.wait(timeout=2)
                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                    pass
                size = os.fstat(fd).st_size
                now = time.time()
                if (size > 0 and not acknowledged) or now - last_beat >= 10:
                    changes = {"bytes": size}
                    if size > 0 and not acknowledged:
                        changes.update(state="recording", started=int(now))
                        acknowledged = True
                        notify_start(self.unprotected)
                    cur = self.beat(**changes)
                    last_beat = now
                else:
                    cur = self.read()
                # its channel's address turned (a playlist that turns its links): the
                # same file goes on from the new one (a few seconds between shows)
                moved = (cur or {}).get("handoff") if r["kind"] == "iptv" else None
                if moved and moved.get("gen") != self.handoff_gen and isinstance(moved.get("url"), str):
                    self.close_input(proc, relay)
                    relay, proc, tail = self.open_input(moved["url"], height, fd)
                    self.handoff_gen, self.url = moved["gen"], moved["url"]
                    self.beat(source={"url": moved["url"]})
                    continue
                if proc.poll() is not None:
                    outcome = "incomplete"
                    reason = classify(tail.text) if tail else "stopped"
                    break
                outcome, reason = self.should_stop(cur, root, size, r["keepFree"])
                if outcome:
                    break
        finally:
            if proc and proc.poll() is None:
                proc.send_signal(signal.SIGINT)
                try:
                    proc.wait(timeout=15)
                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                    proc.kill()
                    proc.wait()
            if relay:
                relay.stop()
            size = os.fstat(fd).st_size if fd is not None else 0
            if fd is not None:
                os.close(fd)
        if size == 0:
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                os.unlink(part, dir_fd=dfd)
            if outcome == "done":
                return None, "", {}      # stopped before anything came: nothing to keep
            return "failed", reason or (classify(tail.text) if tail else "stopped"), {}
        place_file(dfd, part, name)
        write_details(dfd, r, size)
        return outcome or "incomplete", reason, {"bytes": size}

    def open_input(self, upstream, height, fd):
        """The relay and ffmpeg for an address, writing on into fd"""
        relay = relay_module().Relay(upstream, height).start()
        proc = subprocess.Popen(ffmpeg_argv(relay.url), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=fd, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True)
        tail = Tail(proc.stderr)
        tail.start()
        return relay, proc, tail

    def close_input(self, proc, relay):
        if proc and proc.poll() is None:
            proc.send_signal(signal.SIGINT)
            try:
                proc.wait(timeout=15)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                proc.kill()
                proc.wait()
        if relay:
            relay.stop()

    def save_video(self, r, root, dfd):
        work = ".work-" + self.rid
        os.mkdir(work, 0o700, dir_fd=dfd)
        q = r.get("quality", 1080)
        fmt = f"bv*[vcodec^=avc1][height<={q}]+ba[ext=m4a]/bv*[height<={q}]+ba/b[height<={q}]/b"
        out = os.path.join(root, work, "video.%(ext)s")
        argv = [YTDLP, "--ignore-config", "--no-plugin-dirs", "--no-playlist", "--no-progress", "--no-warnings", "-q",
                "--no-mtime", "-f", fmt, "--merge-output-format", "mkv", "-o", out, "--",
                "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=" + r["source"]["video"]]
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True)
        tail = Tail(proc.stderr)
        tail.start()
        acknowledged = False
        outcome = None
        last_beat = 0
        try:
            while proc.poll() is None:
                try:
                    proc.wait(timeout=2)
                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                    pass
                size = work_size(dfd, work)
                media = work_size(dfd, work, media_only=True)
                if (media > 0 and not acknowledged) or time.time() - last_beat >= 10:
                    changes = {"bytes": size}
                    if media > 0 and not acknowledged:
                        # Saving only once video has come (not yt-dlp's notes)
                        changes.update(state="recording", started=int(time.time()))
                        acknowledged = True
                        notify_start(self.unprotected)
                    cur = self.beat(**changes)
                    last_beat = time.time()
                else:
                    cur = self.read()
                stop_now, why = self.should_stop(dict(cur or {}, end=0), root, size, r["keepFree"])
                if stop_now:
                    outcome = (stop_now, why)
                    break
        finally:
            if proc.poll() is None:
                os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGINT)
                try:
                    proc.wait(timeout=15)
                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                    os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
                    proc.wait()
        result = None
        if outcome is None and proc.returncode == 0:
            wfd = os.open(work, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dfd)
            try:
                made = [n for n in os.listdir(wfd) if n.startswith("video.") and not n.endswith((".part", ".ytdl"))
                        and stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(n, dir_fd=wfd).st_mode)]
                if len(made) == 1:
                    name = os.path.splitext(r["file"])[0] + os.path.splitext(made[0])[1]
                    if name != r["file"]:
                        self.beat(file=name)
                        r["file"] = name
                    place_file(dfd, os.path.join(work, made[0]), name)
                    result = os.lstat(name, dir_fd=dfd).st_size
            finally:
                os.close(wfd)
        drop_work(dfd, self.rid)
        if result:
            write_details(dfd, r, result)
            return "done", "", {"bytes": result}
        if outcome and outcome[0] == "done":
            return None, "", {}      # you stopped it: nothing half-saved stays
        return "failed", outcome[1] if outcome else classify(tail.text), {}


def work_size(dfd, work, media_only=False):
    """What's in a video save's work folder; media_only: the video's own
    files (video.*), not yt-dlp's notes (.ytdl)"""
    total = 0
    try:
        wfd = os.open(work, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dfd)
    except OSError:
        return 0
    try:
        for n in os.listdir(wfd):
            if media_only and (not n.startswith("video.") or n.endswith(".ytdl")):
                continue
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                total += os.lstat(n, dir_fd=wfd).st_size
    finally:
        os.close(wfd)
    return total


def write_details(dfd, r, size):
    """What the card shows, next to the recording (never the stream's address)"""
    name = os.path.splitext(r["file"])[0] + ".json"
    details = {"uberTV": 1, "title": r.get("title", ""), "titles": r.get("titles", []), "desc": r.get("desc", ""),
               "category": r.get("category", ""), "channel": {"name": r["channel"].get("name", ""),
               "number": r["channel"].get("number", 0), "hash": r["channel"].get("hash", "")},
               "kind": r["kind"], "video": r.get("video", ""), "start": r.get("started") or r.get("created"),
               "end": int(time.time()), "bytes": size}
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        fd = os.open(name, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600, dir_fd=dfd)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(details, f)


def duration_of(path):
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([FFPROBE, "-v", "error", "-show_entries", "format=duration", "-of", "csv=p=0", path],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30).stdout.strip()
        return round(float(out)) if out else 0
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return 0


def thumb_of(path, rid):
    d = thumbs_dir()
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.makedirs(d, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    out = os.path.join(d, "rec-%s.jpg" % rid)
    try:
        subprocess.run([THUMBNAILER, "-i", path, "-o", out, "-s", "480", "-t", "15%", "-q", "7"], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
        if os.path.getsize(out) > 0:
            os.chmod(out, 0o600)
            return out
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        pass
    return ""


REASONS = {"drive": "the drive isn't there", "readonly": "the drive can't be written to", "space": "the disk got too full",
           "size": "it reached the largest size a recording can be", "refused": "the provider refused the stream",
           "network": "the stream stopped answering", "unreadable": "the stream couldn't be read",
           "stopped": "the stream stopped", "service": "it couldn't start", "offline": "the channel isn't live right now",
           "gone": "its channel isn't in your list anymore", "conflict": "too many recordings at this time",
           "notRunning": "Uber TV wasn't running when it was on (logged out, asleep or off)"}


def notify(r):
    """How it went, in an Omarchy notification: never what it is (a channel
    can be locked while it records); the card in Recordings says"""
    if not r:
        return
    why = REASONS.get(r.get("reason"), "it stopped")
    if r["state"] == "done":
        summary, body = "Recording finished", "It's in Uber TV's Recordings."
    elif r["state"] == "incomplete":
        summary, body = "Recording stopped early", why[0].upper() + why[1:] + ". What was recorded is in Recordings."
    elif r["state"] == "missed":
        summary, body = "Recording missed", why[0].upper() + why[1:] + "."
    elif r["state"] == "conflict":
        summary, body = "Recording didn't start", why[0].upper() + why[1:] + "."
    else:
        summary, body = "Recording failed", why[0].upper() + why[1:] + "."
    say_note(summary, body)


def notify_start(unprotected):
    say_note("Recording", "This computer may go to sleep during it: sleep protection is unavailable." if unprotected
             else "It goes on with Uber TV closed.")


def say_note(summary, body):
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        subprocess.run([NOTIFY, "-a", "Uber TV", summary, body], capture_output=True, timeout=10)


# ---- pause and rewind: the rolling buffer ----

BUF_DIR = ".uber-tv-buffer"
BUF_UNIT = "uber-tv-buf-"
BUF_MINUTES = (5, 30)
BUF_HEIGHTS = (1080, 720, 480)
BUF_LEASE = 20                     # seconds without the guide asking for the status: it's gone
BUF_FIRST_LEASE = 60               # before it first asks
BUF_MARGIN = 512 * 1024 ** 2       # free space on top of Keep free while it writes (MARGIN more with a recording on that drive)
BUF_RESTARTS = 3                   # the writer started again, within BUF_RESTART_SPAN, before the buffer gives up
BUF_RESTART_SPAN = 120
BUF_FILE_RE = re.compile(r"^(s\d{9}\.ts|p\d{1,6}\.m3u8)(\.tmp)?\Z")   # what the writer makes in a session's folder


def buffers_dir():
    d = os.path.join(ensure_state_dir(), "buffers")
    with contextlib.suppress(FileExistsError):
        os.mkdir(d, 0o700)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(d).st_mode):
        raise OSError(errno.ENOTDIR, "the buffers' folder isn't a folder")
    return d


def read_control(session):
    """A session's control file (its address, secret, place, port), or None"""
    try:
        fd = os.open(os.path.join(buffers_dir(), session + ".json"), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        return None
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
        data = f.read(64 * 1024 + 1)
    try:
        c = json.loads(data) if len(data) <= 64 * 1024 else None
    except ValueError:
        c = None
    return c if isinstance(c, dict) else None


def write_control(session, c):
    d = buffers_dir()
    tmp = os.path.join(d, session + ".json.tmp-" + secrets.token_hex(6))
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, json.dumps(c).encode())
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(d, session + ".json"))


def drop_control(session):
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.unlink(os.path.join(buffers_dir(), session + ".json"))


BUF_PROBE_TIMEOUT = 10


def buffer_state(session):
    """A session's service as systemd says: "active", "inactive" (stopped,
    failed or not there), or "unknown" when it can't be asked"""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([SYSTEMCTL, "--user", "show", "-p", "ActiveState", "--value", BUF_UNIT + session],
                             capture_output=True, timeout=BUF_PROBE_TIMEOUT)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return "unknown"
    state = out.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
    if out.returncode != 0 or not state:
        return "unknown"
    return "inactive" if state in ("inactive", "failed") else "active"


def buffer_running(session):
    """Running, or not known to have stopped: only a stop systemd confirms
    lets its folder go or something else use the provider"""
    return buffer_state(session) != "inactive"


def empty_session(bfd, session):
    """A session's folder emptied of what the writer makes (never following a
    link, regular files only) and removed; anything else in it stays"""
    try:
        sfd = os.open(session, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=bfd)
    except OSError:
        return
    try:
        for name in os.listdir(sfd):
            if BUF_FILE_RE.match(name):
                with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                    if stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(name, dir_fd=sfd).st_mode):
                        os.unlink(name, dir_fd=sfd)
    finally:
        os.close(sfd)
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        os.rmdir(session, dir_fd=bfd)


def open_buffers(root, make=True):
    """The place's buffer folder, opened without following links (made if it's missing), or None"""
    rfd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    try:
        if make:
            with contextlib.suppress(FileExistsError):
                os.mkdir(BUF_DIR, 0o700, dir_fd=rfd)
        if not stat.S_ISDIR(os.lstat(BUF_DIR, dir_fd=rfd).st_mode):
            return None
        bfd = os.open(BUF_DIR, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=rfd)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.fchmod(bfd, 0o700)          # yours alone, however it came to be there (where the drive allows)
        return bfd
    finally:
        os.close(rfd)


def clean_buffers(root, keep=""):
    """Sessions left behind (a crash, a drive pulled): their folders, if they're
    at this place, and every control file whose writer isn't running"""
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        for name in os.listdir(buffers_dir()):
            session = name[:-5] if name.endswith(".json") else ""
            if ID_RE.match(session) and session != keep and not buffer_running(session):
                drop_control(session)
    try:
        bfd = open_buffers(root, make=False)
    except OSError:
        return
    if bfd is None:
        return
    try:
        for name in os.listdir(bfd):
            if ID_RE.match(name) and name != keep and not read_control(name):
                empty_session(bfd, name)
    finally:
        os.close(bfd)


def buffer_start(raw):
    """A session started: {"url", "minutes", "place", "keepFree", "height"} on stdin.
    Answers once its server is up: {session, base} (base: its address, secret included)."""
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not relay_module().web(raw.get("url")) or len(str(raw.get("url"))) > 8192:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "url"}
    if raw.get("minutes") not in BUF_MINUTES:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "minutes"}
    try:
        keep = max(GiB, min(100 * GiB, int(raw.get("keepFree", 5 * GiB))))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        keep = 5 * GiB
    height = raw.get("height") if raw.get("height") in BUF_HEIGHTS else 1080
    root, problem = verify(raw.get("place"))
    if not root:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "drive"}
    if problem:
        return {"ok": False, "error": problem}
    if free_of(root) < keep + MARGIN:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "space"}
    clean_buffers(root)
    session, secret = secrets.token_hex(8), secrets.token_urlsafe(24)
    write_control(session, {"session": session, "secret": secret, "url": raw["url"], "minutes": raw["minutes"],
                            "keepFree": keep, "height": height, "place": raw["place"], "port": 0, "created": int(time.time())})
    argv = [SYSTEMD_RUN, "--user", "--quiet", "--collect", "--unit=" + BUF_UNIT + session, "--service-type=exec",
            "--expand-environment=no", "--description=Uber TV pause and rewind", "-p", "MemoryMax=384M", "-p", "CPUWeight=20",
            "-p", "KillMode=mixed", "-p", "TimeoutStopSec=15", "-p", "RuntimeMaxSec=86400"]
    for var in ("XDG_CONFIG_HOME", "XDG_CACHE_HOME"):
        if os.environ.get(var, "").startswith("/"):
            argv.append("--setenv=%s=%s" % (var, os.environ[var]))
    argv += ["--", PYTHON, "-I", os.path.realpath(__file__), "buffer-run", session]
    try:
        ok = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, timeout=30).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        ok = False
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 10
    while ok and time.monotonic() < deadline:
        c = read_control(session)
        if not c or c.get("failed"):
            break
        if c.get("port"):
            return {"ok": True, "session": session, "base": "http://127.0.0.1:%d/%s" % (c["port"], secret)}
        time.sleep(0.05)
    c = read_control(session) or {}
    buffer_stop(session)
    return {"ok": False, "error": c.get("failed") if c.get("failed") in ("drive", "readonly", "space") else "service"}


def buffer_stop(session):
    """A session stopped, its writer gone (the provider's stream closed) before
    it answers ok, its folder deleted. Still running after the stop and a kill:
    not ok, nothing deleted (asked again, or its lease ends it)"""
    unit = BUF_UNIT + session
    try:
        subprocess.run([SYSTEMCTL, "--user", "stop", unit], capture_output=True, timeout=40)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        pass
    if buffer_running(session):
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            subprocess.run([SYSTEMCTL, "--user", "kill", "--signal=SIGKILL", unit], capture_output=True, timeout=10)
        deadline = time.monotonic() + 10
        while buffer_running(session) and time.monotonic() < deadline:
            time.sleep(0.2)
        if buffer_running(session):
            return {"ok": False, "error": "running"}
    c = read_control(session)
    if c:   # the writer didn't clean up after itself (it was killed): its folder and control file
        root, _ = verify(c.get("place"))
        if root:
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                bfd = open_buffers(root, make=False)
                if bfd is not None:
                    try:
                        empty_session(bfd, session)
                    finally:
                        os.close(bfd)
        drop_control(session)
    return {"ok": True}


def buffer_follow(session, raw):
    """A session's channel at a new address (a playlist that turned its links):
    the writer closes the old one, then opens it"""
    if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not relay_module().web(raw.get("url")) or len(str(raw.get("url"))) > 8192:
        return {"ok": False, "error": "url"}
    with locked():
        c = read_control(session)
        if not c:
            return {"ok": False, "error": "unknown"}
        if c.get("url") == raw["url"] and not c.get("handoff"):
            return {"ok": True, "same": True}
        gen = int((c.get("handoff") or {}).get("gen", 0)) + 1
        c["handoff"] = {"url": raw["url"], "gen": gen}
        write_control(session, c)
    return {"ok": True, "gen": gen}


def buffer_argv(url, fd, start, run):
    """ffmpeg copying the channel from the relay into the session's folder (by its
    fd: a drive that's gone fails, never sends it elsewhere) as 2 s segments"""
    d = "/proc/self/fd/%d/" % fd
    return [FFMPEG, "-nostdin", "-hide_banner", "-loglevel", "error",
            "-protocol_whitelist", "http,https,tcp,tls,crypto",
            "-reconnect", "1", "-reconnect_streamed", "1", "-reconnect_on_network_error", "1",
            "-reconnect_delay_max", "10", "-rw_timeout", "20000000",
            "-i", url, "-map", "0:v:0?", "-map", "0:a:0?", "-c", "copy",
            "-f", "hls", "-hls_time", "2", "-hls_list_size", "3000", "-hls_flags", "temp_file",
            "-start_number", str(start), "-hls_segment_filename", d + "s%09d.ts", d + "p%d.m3u8" % run]


class BufferWorker:
    def __init__(self, session, clock=time.monotonic, signals=True):
        self.session = session
        self.clock = clock
        self.stopping = False
        self.state = "filling"
        self.reason = ""
        self.proc = None
        self.relay = None
        self.tail = None
        self.run_no = 0
        self.gen = 0
        self.restarts = []
        self.restart_at = None             # when the writer starts again, after it stopped
        self.relays = relay_module()
        for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP) if signals else ():
            signal.signal(s, self.on_signal)

    def on_signal(self, *args):
        self.stopping = True

    def part(self):
        return {"state": "failed" if self.reason else self.state, "reason": self.reason}

    def open_writer(self, url, height, sfd, buf):
        self.run_no += 1
        try:
            self.relay = self.relays.Relay(url, height).start()
            self.proc = subprocess.Popen(buffer_argv(self.relay.url, sfd, buf.next_seq(), self.run_no), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                         stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True, pass_fds=(sfd,))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self.fail("service")
            return
        self.tail = Tail(self.proc.stderr)
        self.tail.start()

    def close_writer(self):
        if self.proc and self.proc.poll() is None:
            self.proc.send_signal(signal.SIGINT)
            try:
                self.proc.wait(timeout=5)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                self.proc.kill()
                self.proc.wait()
        if self.relay:
            self.relay.stop()
        self.proc = self.relay = None

    def fail(self, reason):
        """Gives up: the provider's stream closed at once; the status says why until the guide stops it"""
        self.close_writer()
        self.reason = reason

    @staticmethod
    def free(fd):
        s = os.fstatvfs(fd)
        return s.f_bavail * s.f_frsize

    def recording_there(self, place):
        """A recording running on the same drive (the buffer stops well before it would)"""
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            for r in load()["recordings"].values():
                if r.get("state") in ACTIVE and (r.get("place") or {}).get("volume") == place.get("volume"):
                    return True
        return False

    def run(self):
        os.umask(0o077)
        c = read_control(self.session)
        if not c:
            return
        root, problem = verify(c.get("place"))
        if not root or problem:
            c["failed"] = problem or "drive"
            write_control(self.session, c)
            return
        bfd = sfd = server = None
        try:
            bfd = open_buffers(root)
            if bfd is None:
                raise OSError(errno.ENOTDIR, "not a folder")
            os.mkdir(self.session, 0o700, dir_fd=bfd)
            sfd = os.open(self.session, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=bfd)
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                os.fchmod(sfd, 0o700)
            mod = buffer_module()
            buf = mod.Buffer(sfd, c["minutes"], self.clock)
            server = mod.Server(buf, c["secret"], self.part, self.clock).start()
        except OSError:
            c["failed"] = "drive"
            write_control(self.session, c)
            time.sleep(2)   # long enough for whoever started it to read why
        else:
            c["port"] = server.port
            write_control(self.session, c)
            self.loop(c, root, sfd, buf, server, mod.PLAYLIST_MAX)
        finally:
            self.close_writer()
            if server:
                server.stop()
            if sfd is not None:
                os.close(sfd)
            if bfd is not None:
                empty_session(bfd, self.session)
                os.close(bfd)
            drop_control(self.session)

    def loop(self, c, root, sfd, buf, server, most):
        url, height, keep, place = c["url"], c["height"], c["keepFree"], c["place"]
        started = self.clock()
        next_space = next_drive = next_control = 0
        near_recording = self.recording_there(place)
        self.open_writer(url, height, sfd, buf)
        while not self.stopping:
            now = self.clock()
            asked = server.asked > started
            if now - server.asked > (BUF_LEASE if asked else BUF_FIRST_LEASE):
                return                     # the guide is gone
            if not self.reason:
                try:
                    pfd = os.open("p%d.m3u8" % self.run_no, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=sfd)
                    with os.fdopen(pfd, "rb") as f:
                        text = f.read(most).decode("utf-8", "replace")
                    if buf.ingest(text):
                        self.state = "ready" if buf.status()["ready"] else "filling"
                except OSError:
                    pass
                if now >= next_space:
                    next_space = now + 2
                    try:
                        if self.free(sfd) < keep + BUF_MARGIN + (MARGIN if near_recording else 0):
                            self.fail("space")
                    except OSError:
                        self.fail("drive")
                if not self.reason and now >= next_drive:
                    next_drive = now + 10
                    near_recording = self.recording_there(place)
                    there, _ = verify(place)
                    if there != root:
                        self.fail("drive")
                if not self.reason and now >= next_control:
                    next_control = now + 1
                    moved = (read_control(self.session) or {}).get("handoff")
                    if isinstance(moved, dict) and isinstance(moved.get("gen"), int) and moved["gen"] > self.gen \
                            and self.relays.web(moved.get("url")):
                        self.close_writer()          # the old address closed before the new one opens
                        self.gen, url = moved["gen"], moved["url"]
                        buf.restarted()
                        self.restart_at = None
                        self.open_writer(url, height, sfd, buf)
                if not self.reason and self.proc and self.proc.poll() is not None:
                    why = classify(self.tail.text) if self.tail else "stopped"
                    self.restarts = [t for t in self.restarts if now - t < BUF_RESTART_SPAN] + [now]
                    self.close_writer()
                    if len(self.restarts) > BUF_RESTARTS:
                        self.fail(why)
                    else:
                        self.restart_at = now + min(8, 2 ** len(self.restarts))
                if not self.reason and self.restart_at is not None and now >= self.restart_at:
                    self.restart_at = None
                    buf.restarted()
                    self.open_writer(url, height, sfd, buf)
            time.sleep(0.5)


def main(argv):
    if len(argv) < 2:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    cmd, args = argv[1], argv[2:]
    if cmd == "drives" and not args:
        say({"ok": True, "drives": drives()})
    elif cmd == "check" and len(args) == 1:
        c = check_place(args[0])
        say({"ok": False, "error": c["error"]} if "error" in c else dict(c, ok=True, free=free_of(c["path"]), size=size_of(c["path"])))
    elif cmd == "prepare" and (len(args) == 1 or (len(args) == 2 and args[1] == "make")):
        say(prepare(args[0], len(args) == 2))
    elif cmd == "where" and not args:
        try:
            place = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            place = None
        say(where(place))
    elif cmd == "mount" and len(args) == 1:
        say(mount_drive(args[0]))
    elif cmd == "start" and not args:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(64 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(start(raw))
    elif cmd == "schedule" and not args:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(512 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(schedule(raw))
    elif cmd == "series" and args == ["add"]:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(series_add(raw))
    elif cmd == "series" and len(args) == 2 and args[0] == "remove" and ID_RE.match(args[1]):
        say(series_remove(args[1]))
    elif cmd == "cancel" and len(args) == 1 and ID_RE.match(args[0]):
        say(cancel(args[0]))
    elif cmd == "limit" and len(args) == 1 and args[0] in ("1", "2", "3", "4"):
        say(limit(int(args[0])))
    elif cmd == "clear" and not args:
        say(clear())
    elif cmd == "follow" and not args:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(follow_cmd(raw))
    elif cmd == "tag" and not args:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(tag(raw))
    elif cmd in ("stop", "remove") and len(args) == 1 and ID_RE.match(args[0]):
        say(stop(args[0]) if cmd == "stop" else remove(args[0]))
    elif cmd == "until" and len(args) == 2 and ID_RE.match(args[0]) and args[1].isdigit():
        say(until(args[0], int(args[1])))
    elif cmd == "list" and not args:
        say(listing())
    elif cmd == "run" and len(args) == 1 and ID_RE.match(args[0]):
        Worker(args[0]).run()
    elif cmd == "buffer" and args == ["start"]:
        try:
            raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
        except ValueError:
            raw = None
        say(buffer_start(raw))
    elif cmd == "buffer" and len(args) == 2 and args[0] in ("stop", "follow") and ID_RE.match(args[1]):
        if args[0] == "stop":
            say(buffer_stop(args[1]))
        else:
            try:
                raw = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(16 * 1024))
            except ValueError:
                raw = None
            say(buffer_follow(args[1], raw))
    elif cmd == "buffer-run" and len(args) == 1 and ID_RE.match(args[0]):
        BufferWorker(args[0]).run()
    else:
        sys.exit(__doc__)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main(sys.argv)
    except BrokenPipeError:
        pass
